{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/middleware.cljc | sed -n '1,540p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.middleware\n     2\t  \"DaoStream middleware: a handle-level adapter value, one `in` transform\n     3\t   over the operation map and one `out` transform over the outcome map\n     4\t   (docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md).\n     5\t\n     6\t   A middleware is a value, never a callback: every transform here is\n     7\t   called downward by the caller and returns at once. `wrap` composes a\n     8\t   chain over a handle; `apply-request` is the one place an operation map\n     9\t   becomes a protocol call; `gate` and `present` are the two generic\n    10\t   middlewares; `encryption` and `metering` are the spec's exemplars;\n    11\t   `channel-allow-list` is the trivial policy this repository ships with.\n    12\t\n    13\t   The position rule is structural, not a convention: `wrap` validates\n    14\t   every `out` result against the permitted changes and raises on a\n    15\t   violation, so a filter cannot be expressed. Each transform is still\n    16\t   total, returns at once, never loops, retries, waits or touches the\n    17\t   inner handle, and maps inner position p to outer position p.\"\n    18\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\t;; =============================================================================\n    22\t;; The one dispatch point\n    23\t;; =============================================================================\n    24\t\n    25\t(defn- dispatch\n    26\t  \"Apply one operation map to a plain handle: the place an operation map\n    27\t   becomes a protocol call. An op outside the middleware vocabulary\n    28\t   (cursor, next, append!) is a defect in the host's own assembly -- the\n    29\t   mirror validates ops before this -- so it throws, per the contract's\n    30\t   reservation of exceptions (dao.stream.md, Result Convention).\"\n    31\t  [h req]\n    32\t  (let [[arg] (:dao.stream.remote/args req)]\n    33\t    (case (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n    34\t      :dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h arg)\n    35\t      :dao.stream/next (stream/next h arg)\n    36\t      :dao.stream/append! (stream/append! h arg)\n    37\t      (throw (ex-info \"dao.stream.middleware: unknown operation\"\n    38\t                      {:op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)})))))\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(defprotocol IMiddlewareHandle\n    42\t  \"Internal seam of this namespace: the handle `wrap` returns answers one\n    43\t   whole chain pass under a caller-supplied context. `apply-request` uses\n    44\t   it so a composition (the mirror step of dao.stream.remote.md) can run\n    45\t   a table entry's middleware with its own context, exactly as the\n    46\t   wrapped handle's protocol methods run it with the local caller's {}.\n    47\t   Call `apply-request`, never this.\"\n    48\t\n    49\t  (operate-through\n    50\t    [handle ctx req]\n    51\t    \"Run the wrapped chain for operation map `req` under `ctx`.\"))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn apply-request\n    55\t  \"Applies one operation map to a handle: `(apply-request h ctx req) ->\n    56\t   outcome`. On a plain handle this is the protocol call and `ctx` is\n    57\t   unused. On a handle `wrap` returned, this is the whole chain pass\n    58\t   under `ctx`: the entry point the mirror step composes with a channel\n    59\t   context. Extra qualified keys on `req` pass through untouched.\"\n    60\t  [h ctx req]\n    61\t  (if (satisfies? IMiddlewareHandle h)\n    62\t    (operate-through h ctx req)\n    63\t    (dispatch h req)))\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\t;; =============================================================================\n    67\t;; wrap\n    68\t;; =============================================================================\n    69\t\n    70\t(def ^:private position-keys\n    71\t  \"The outcome keys an `out` result may never change: the outcome kind,\n    72\t   the stream identity, and every key naming the operation, the request\n    73\t   id or a position -- a cursor, an anchor or a gap recovery cursor.\n    74\t   Adding any of these where the outcome had none is a change too.\"\n    75\t  [:dao.stream/outcome\n    76\t   :dao.stream/cursor\n    77\t   :dao.stream/anchor\n    78\t   :dao.stream/identity\n    79\t   :dao.stream.remote/op\n    80\t   :dao.stream.remote/id])\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(defn- position-preserving?\n    84\t  \"True when `result`, the outcome an `out` transform returns for the\n    85\t   `outcome` it received, makes none of the changes the position rule\n    86\t   forbids: no key of the outcome is dropped, the outcome kind, the\n    87\t   identity, the operation, the request id and every cursor, anchor and\n    88\t   gap recovery cursor are unchanged, and -- except for `next`'s\n    89\t   :dao.stream/value on :dao.stream/ok, the one replacement a value\n    90\t   transform owns -- the value is unchanged. Open keys may be added.\n    91\t   Structural checks over the two outcome maps only, never a walk over\n    92\t   elements.\"\n    93\t  [req outcome result]\n    94\t  (and (map? result)\n    95\t       (every? #(contains? result %) (keys outcome))\n    96\t       (every? (fn [k] (= (get outcome k) (get result k)))\n    97\t               position-keys)\n    98\t       (or (and (= :dao.stream/next (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n    99\t                (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result)))\n   100\t           (= (get outcome :dao.stream/value)\n   101\t              (get result :dao.stream/value)))))\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t(defn- run-outs\n   105\t  \"Run every `out` transform from the innermost outward over `outcome`,\n   106\t   for the middlewares at chain indices below `upto`. Each result is\n   107\t   validated against the position rule: an `out` that changes anything\n   108\t   beyond the permitted replacements is a defect in the host's own\n   109\t   assembly of the chain and raises, per the contract's reservation of\n   110\t   exceptions (dao.stream.md, Result Convention) -- a filter is then\n   111\t   impossible, not merely discouraged.\"\n   112\t  [chain ctx req outcome upto]\n   113\t  (reduce\n   114\t    (fn [out i]\n   115\t      (let [result ((:dao.stream.middleware/out (nth chain i))\n   116\t                    ctx req out)]\n   117\t        (if (position-preserving? req out result)\n   118\t          result\n   119\t          (throw (ex-info \"dao.stream.middleware: out broke the position rule\"\n   120\t                          {:middleware i\n   121\t                           :op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n   122\t                           :received out\n   123\t                           :returned result})))))\n   124\t    outcome\n   125\t    (range (dec upto) -1 -1)))\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\t(defn- operate\n   129\t  \"One pass of `chain` over `req` under `ctx`: every `in` from the\n   130\t   outermost inward, the final request applied to `h` with\n   131\t   `apply-request` (which recurses into an inner wrapped handle, so\n   132\t   `ctx` carries through nesting), every `out` from the innermost\n   133\t   outward. An `in` answering an outcome map short-circuits: the inner\n   134\t   handle is not consulted and only the middlewares outside it\n   135\t   transform the outcome.\"\n   136\t  [h chain ctx req]\n   137\t  (loop [i 0, req req]\n   138\t    (if (= i (count chain))\n   139\t      (run-outs chain ctx req (apply-request h ctx req) (count chain))\n   140\t      (let [res ((:dao.stream.middleware/in (nth chain i)) ctx req)]\n   141\t        (if (stream/outcome-map? res)\n   142\t          (run-outs chain ctx req res i)\n   143\t          (recur (inc i) res))))))\n   144\t\n   145\t\n   146\t(defn- instantiated\n   147\t  \"Instantiate one middleware of a chain at wrap: when its definition\n   148\t   declares a `:dao.stream.middleware/state` constructor, `wrap` calls\n   149\t   it once, here, and specializes the definition's transforms to the\n   150\t   state minted. The state is therefore state of the wrapped handle --\n   151\t   one definition wrapped over two handles holds two states, each\n   152\t   minted by its own wrap (dao.stream.middleware.md, gate). A\n   153\t   definition that declares no constructor wraps as it is.\"\n   154\t  [mw]\n   155\t  (if-some [make (:dao.stream.middleware/state mw)]\n   156\t    (let [s (make)]\n   157\t      {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   158\t       (fn [ctx req] ((:dao.stream.middleware/in mw) s ctx req))\n   159\t       :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   160\t       (fn [ctx req out] ((:dao.stream.middleware/out mw) s ctx req out))})\n   161\t    mw))\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\t(defn wrap\n   165\t  \"Compose `chain`, a vector of middleware values applied outermost\n   166\t   first, over handle `h`. The returned handle implements exactly the\n   167\t   protocols `h` implements -- descriptor, which every handle carries,\n   168\t   plus its reader, writer and closable surfaces. On each protocol call\n   169\t   it builds the operation map, runs every `in` outermost inward,\n   170\t   applies the result to `h` with `apply-request` under the local\n   171\t   caller's {} context, and runs every `out` innermost outward, each\n   172\t   `out` result validated against the position rule -- a result beyond\n   173\t   the permitted changes raises, so a filter cannot hide in a chain.\n   174\t   `wrap` also mints each middleware definition's declared state once,\n   175\t   here, so that state belongs to this wrapped handle. `descriptor` and\n   176\t   `close!` delegate to `h` unchanged: no middleware sees them. The\n   177\t   surface branches below are plain reify forms, one per combination,\n   178\t   because a handle implements its surface and no other.\"\n   179\t  [h chain]\n   180\t  (let [chain (mapv instantiated chain)\n   181\t        flow (fn [ctx req] (operate h chain ctx req))\n   182\t        r? (stream/reader? h)\n   183\t        w? (stream/writer? h)\n   184\t        c? (stream/closable? h)]\n   185\t    (cond\n   186\t      (and r? w? c?)\n   187\t      (reify\n   188\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   189\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   190\t\n   191\t\n   192\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   193\t\n   194\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   195\t\n   196\t\n   197\t        stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   198\t\n   199\t        (cursor\n   200\t          [_ anchor]\n   201\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   202\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [anchor]}))\n   203\t\n   204\t        (next\n   205\t          [_ c]\n   206\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   207\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [c]}))\n   208\t\n   209\t\n   210\t        stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   211\t\n   212\t        (append!\n   213\t          [_ v]\n   214\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   215\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [v]}))\n   216\t\n   217\t\n   218\t        stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   219\t\n   220\t        (close! [_] (stream/close! h)))\n   221\t\n   222\t      (and r? w?)\n   223\t      (reify\n   224\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   225\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   226\t\n   227\t\n   228\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   229\t\n   230\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   231\t\n   232\t\n   233\t        stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   234\t\n   235\t        (cursor\n   236\t          [_ anchor]\n   237\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   238\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [anchor]}))\n   239\t\n   240\t        (next\n   241\t          [_ c]\n   242\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   243\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [c]}))\n   244\t\n   245\t\n   246\t        stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   247\t\n   248\t        (append!\n   249\t          [_ v]\n   250\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   251\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [v]})))\n   252\t\n   253\t      (and r? c?)\n   254\t      (reify\n   255\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   256\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   257\t\n   258\t\n   259\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   260\t\n   261\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   262\t\n   263\t\n   264\t        stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   265\t\n   266\t        (cursor\n   267\t          [_ anchor]\n   268\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   269\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [anchor]}))\n   270\t\n   271\t        (next\n   272\t          [_ c]\n   273\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   274\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [c]}))\n   275\t\n   276\t\n   277\t        stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   278\t\n   279\t        (close! [_] (stream/close! h)))\n   280\t\n   281\t      (and w? c?)\n   282\t      (reify\n   283\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   284\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   288\t\n   289\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   290\t\n   291\t\n   292\t        stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   293\t\n   294\t        (append!\n   295\t          [_ v]\n   296\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   297\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [v]}))\n   298\t\n   299\t\n   300\t        stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   301\t\n   302\t        (close! [_] (stream/close! h)))\n   303\t\n   304\t      r?\n   305\t      (reify\n   306\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   307\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   308\t\n   309\t\n   310\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   311\t\n   312\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   313\t\n   314\t\n   315\t        stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   316\t\n   317\t        (cursor\n   318\t          [_ anchor]\n   319\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   320\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [anchor]}))\n   321\t\n   322\t        (next\n   323\t          [_ c]\n   324\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   325\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [c]})))\n   326\t\n   327\t      w?\n   328\t      (reify\n   329\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   330\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   331\t\n   332\t\n   333\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   334\t\n   335\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   336\t\n   337\t\n   338\t        stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   339\t\n   340\t        (append!\n   341\t          [_ v]\n   342\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   343\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [v]})))\n   344\t\n   345\t      c?\n   346\t      (reify\n   347\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   348\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   349\t\n   350\t\n   351\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   352\t\n   353\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   354\t\n   355\t\n   356\t        stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   357\t\n   358\t        (close! [_] (stream/close! h)))\n   359\t\n   360\t      :else\n   361\t      (reify\n   362\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   363\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   364\t\n   365\t\n   366\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   367\t\n   368\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))))))\n   369\t\n   370\t\n   371\t;; =============================================================================\n   372\t;; gate, the authorize step\n   373\t;; =============================================================================\n   374\t\n   375\t(def ^:private none-marker\n   376\t  \"The decision `verify` receives when the gate has none: no minted\n   377\t   cursor, no value observed yet, or a value cleared by a failed read.\n   378\t   A policy that must fail closed refuses it.\"\n   379\t  {:dao.stream.middleware/none true})\n   380\t\n   381\t\n   382\t(def ^:private ended-marker\n   383\t  \"The decision `verify` receives once the gate is ended: the medium\n   384\t   answered end, so no later operation reads it.\"\n   385\t  {:dao.stream.middleware/ended true})\n   386\t\n   387\t\n   388\t(defn gate\n   389\t  \"The authorize step: `(gate {:dao.stream.middleware/verify verify\n   390\t   :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})` -> middleware definition.\n   391\t   `wrap` mints the gate's state once per wrapped handle and, minting\n   392\t   it, calls `cursor` :oldest on the decision medium once: the read\n   393\t   cursor and the last value are state of the wrapped handle, so one\n   394\t   definition may be wrapped over many handles, each with its own\n   395\t   cursor. Each operation retries the mint once when it has no cursor,\n   396\t   then calls `next` on the medium once, plus the one recovery re-read\n   397\t   after a gap; when the medium answers end the gate becomes ended and\n   398\t   reads no more. `verify` is `(fn [decision ctx req] -> nil |\n   399\t   reason)`, the adapter contract of dao.shibi.md: nil passes the\n   400\t   request through; a reason short-circuits with :dao.stream/refused.\n   401\t   Serialize calls on one wrapped handle; the gate has no queue, lock\n   402\t   or wait.\"\n   403\t  [opts]\n   404\t  (let [verify (:dao.stream.middleware/verify opts)\n   405\t        decision (:dao.stream.middleware/decision opts)\n   406\t        blank {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? false}\n   407\t        mint!\n   408\t        (fn []\n   409\t          (let [r (stream/cursor decision stream/anchor-oldest)]\n   410\t            (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   411\t              (:dao.stream/cursor r))))\n   412\t\n   413\t        store! (fn [state s] (vreset! state s) s)\n   414\t\n   415\t        absorb\n   416\t        (fn [s r]\n   417\t          (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   418\t            :dao.stream/ok\n   419\t            {:cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r) :value? true\n   420\t             :value (:dao.stream/value r) :ended? false}\n   421\t\n   422\t            :dao.stream/blocked s\n   423\t\n   424\t            :dao.stream/end\n   425\t            {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? true}\n   426\t\n   427\t            :dao.stream/gap\n   428\t            ;; One recovery re-read; never a third read this operation.\n   429\t            (let [rec (:dao.stream/cursor r)\n   430\t                  r2 (stream/next decision rec)]\n   431\t              (case (:dao.stream/outcome r2)\n   432\t                :dao.stream/ok\n   433\t                {:cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r2) :value? true\n   434\t                 :value (:dao.stream/value r2) :ended? false}\n   435\t\n   436\t                :dao.stream/blocked\n   437\t                {:cursor rec :value? false :value nil :ended? false}\n   438\t\n   439\t                :dao.stream/end\n   440\t                {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? true}\n   441\t\n   442\t                ;; A recovery gap adopts the recovery cursor and stays\n   443\t                ;; without a value.\n   444\t                :dao.stream/gap\n   445\t                {:cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r2) :value? false\n   446\t                 :value nil :ended? false}\n   447\t\n   448\t                ;; Any other recovery outcome clears cursor and value;\n   449\t                ;; the mint is retried afresh next operation.\n   450\t                {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? false}))\n   451\t\n   452\t            ;; Any other non-ok outcome clears value and cursor; the\n   453\t            ;; mint is retried afresh next operation.\n   454\t            {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? false}))\n   455\t\n   456\t        latest\n   457\t        (fn [state]\n   458\t          (let [s0 @state]\n   459\t            (if (:ended? s0)\n   460\t              ended-marker\n   461\t              (do\n   462\t                (when-not (:cursor s0)\n   463\t                  (when-let [c (mint!)]\n   464\t                    (store! state (assoc s0 :cursor c))))\n   465\t                (let [s1 @state]\n   466\t                  (when (:cursor s1)\n   467\t                    (store! state (absorb s1 (stream/next decision\n   468\t                                                          (:cursor s1)))))\n   469\t                  (let [s2 @state]\n   470\t                    (cond (:ended? s2) ended-marker\n   471\t                          (:value? s2) (:value s2)\n   472\t                          :else none-marker)))))))]\n   473\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/state\n   474\t     (fn []\n   475\t       (let [state (volatile! blank)]\n   476\t         (when-let [c (mint!)]\n   477\t           (vswap! state assoc :cursor c))\n   478\t         state))\n   479\t     :dao.stream.middleware/in\n   480\t     (fn [state ctx req]\n   481\t       (let [reason (verify (latest state) ctx req)]\n   482\t         (if (nil? reason)\n   483\t           req\n   484\t           {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/refused\n   485\t            :dao.stream.middleware/reason reason})))\n   486\t     :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   487\t     (fn [_state _ctx _req outcome] outcome)}))\n   488\t\n   489\t\n   490\t;; =============================================================================\n   491\t;; present, the credential step\n   492\t;; =============================================================================\n   493\t\n   494\t(defn present\n   495\t  \"The credential step: `(present {:dao.stream.middleware/present f})`\n   496\t   -> middleware, where `f` is `(fn [ctx req] -> credential)`. Its `in`\n   497\t   associates the result under :dao.stream.remote/credential on the\n   498\t   operation map; its `out` is identity.\"\n   499\t  [opts]\n   500\t  (let [present-fn (:dao.stream.middleware/present opts)]\n   501\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   502\t     (fn [ctx req]\n   503\t       (assoc req :dao.stream.remote/credential (present-fn ctx req)))\n   504\t     :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   505\t     (fn [_ctx _req outcome] outcome)}))\n   506\t\n   507\t\n   508\t;; =============================================================================\n   509\t;; Exemplars\n   510\t;; =============================================================================\n   511\t\n   512\t(defn encryption\n   513\t  \"The spec's value-encryption exemplar. `encipher` and `decipher` come\n   514\t   from a library cipher; the key is an argument to whatever built them.\n   515\t   `in` on append! replaces the value with its ciphertext, answering\n   516\t   :dao.stream/invalid-value when the value cannot be transformed on the\n   517\t   way in. `out` on an ok from next replaces :dao.stream/value with the\n   518\t   plaintext or, when it cannot be transformed on the way out, with\n   519\t   {:dao.stream.middleware/undecodable true :dao.stream.middleware/raw\n   520\t   v}, the outcome and cursor untouched. Cursors are never touched.\"\n   521\t  [opts]\n   522\t  (let [encipher (:dao.stream.middleware/encipher opts)\n   523\t        decipher (:dao.stream.middleware/decipher opts)]\n   524\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   525\t     (fn [_ctx req]\n   526\t       (if (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n   527\t         (try\n   528\t           (update-in req [:dao.stream.remote/args 0] encipher)\n   529\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) _\n   530\t             {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-value}))\n   531\t         req))\n   532\t     :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   533\t     (fn [_ctx req outcome]\n   534\t       (if (and (= :dao.stream/next (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n   535\t                (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)))\n   536\t         (try\n   537\t           (update outcome :dao.stream/value decipher)\n   538\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) _\n   539\t             (assoc outcome :dao.stream/value\n   540\t                    {:dao.stream.middleware/undecodable true\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/dao/stream/middleware_test.cljc | sed -n '1,610p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/dao/stream/middleware_test.cljc | sed -n '1,610p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.middleware-test\n     2\t  \"The middleware slice: the position rule under a value cipher over a\n     3\t   ring buffer; the allow-list gate refusing with :dao.stream/refused; a\n     4\t   gate reading the latest decision through a capacity-1 medium after\n     5\t   eviction; a filter that cannot be expressed, a violating out\n     6\t   raising; and the operation rules of apply-request and wrap, the\n     7\t   short-circuit ordering, the failure markers, the gate's wrap-minted\n     8\t   decision-read lifecycle, metering and present.\"\n     9\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    10\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    11\t            [dao.stream.middleware :as mw]\n    12\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]))\n    13\t\n    14\t\n    15\t;; =============================================================================\n    16\t;; Test support\n    17\t;; =============================================================================\n    18\t\n    19\t(defn- ring\n    20\t  \"An open owner ring-buffer handle with the given capacity.\"\n    21\t  [capacity]\n    22\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    23\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\n    24\t                         :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity})))\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\t(defn- drain-values\n    28\t  \"Every retained value of `h`, oldest first, by a fresh cursor walk.\"\n    29\t  [h]\n    30\t  (loop [c (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest))\n    31\t         acc []]\n    32\t    (let [r (stream/next h c)]\n    33\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n    34\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc (:dao.stream/value r)))\n    35\t        acc))))\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\t(defn- encipher\n    39\t  \"The test cipher's encipher half: a tagged map, total and invertible.\"\n    40\t  [v]\n    41\t  {:cipher/of v})\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(defn- decipher\n    45\t  \"The test cipher's decipher half: it throws on anything that is not\n    46\t   its own ciphertext, as a library cipher fails on a corrupt value.\"\n    47\t  [v]\n    48\t  (if (and (map? v) (contains? v :cipher/of))\n    49\t    (:cipher/of v)\n    50\t    (throw (ex-info \"undecipherable\" {:value v}))))\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t(defn- encryption\n    54\t  \"The spec's value-encryption exemplar over the test cipher.\"\n    55\t  []\n    56\t  (mw/encryption {:dao.stream.middleware/encipher encipher\n    57\t                  :dao.stream.middleware/decipher decipher}))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(defn- recording-handle\n    61\t  \"A reader, writer and closable handle recording every protocol call in\n    62\t   `calls` and answering fixed contract-valid outcomes.\"\n    63\t  [calls]\n    64\t  (reify\n    65\t    stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n    66\t    (descriptor\n    67\t      [_]\n    68\t      (swap! calls conj :descriptor)\n    69\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n    70\t       :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :test/only\n    71\t                               :dao.stream/identity :inner}\n    72\t       :dao.stream/identity :inner})\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t    stream/IDaoStreamReader\n    76\t\n    77\t    (cursor\n    78\t      [_ anchor]\n    79\t      (swap! calls conj [:cursor anchor])\n    80\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor :minted})\n    81\t\n    82\t    (next\n    83\t      [_ c]\n    84\t      (swap! calls conj [:next c])\n    85\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n    86\t       :dao.stream/value :inner-value\n    87\t       :dao.stream/cursor :successor})\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t    stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n    91\t\n    92\t    (append!\n    93\t      [_ v]\n    94\t      (swap! calls conj [:append! v])\n    95\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t    stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n    99\t\n   100\t    (close!\n   101\t      [_]\n   102\t      (swap! calls conj :close!)\n   103\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(defn- spy\n   107\t  \"A middleware recording [:in name] / [:out name] in `log` around the\n   108\t   given transform behavior.\"\n   109\t  [name log in-fn out-fn]\n   110\t  {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   111\t   (fn [ctx req] (swap! log conj [:in name]) (in-fn ctx req))\n   112\t   :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   113\t   (fn [ctx req outcome]\n   114\t     (swap! log conj [:out name])\n   115\t     (out-fn ctx req outcome))})\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(defn- pass-in\n   119\t  [_ctx req]\n   120\t  req)\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- pass-out\n   124\t  [_ctx _req outcome]\n   125\t  outcome)\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\t(defn- refuse-in\n   129\t  \"An `in` that short-circuits with a refused outcome naming `reason`.\"\n   130\t  [reason]\n   131\t  (fn [_ctx _req]\n   132\t    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/refused\n   133\t     :dao.stream.middleware/reason reason}))\n   134\t\n   135\t\n   136\t(defn- scripted-medium\n   137\t  \"A reader-only decision medium: each `cursor` and `next` call is\n   138\t   recorded in `calls` and answered by popping the head of the matching\n   139\t   queue atom.\"\n   140\t  [calls cursors reads]\n   141\t  (reify\n   142\t    stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   143\t    (cursor\n   144\t      [_ anchor]\n   145\t      (swap! calls conj [:cursor anchor])\n   146\t      (let [[r & more] @cursors]\n   147\t        (reset! cursors more)\n   148\t        r))\n   149\t\n   150\t    (next\n   151\t      [_ c]\n   152\t      (swap! calls conj [:next c])\n   153\t      (let [[r & more] @reads]\n   154\t        (reset! reads more)\n   155\t        r))))\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t(defn- ok-cursor\n   159\t  \"A scripted :ok cursor answer for `c`.\"\n   160\t  [c]\n   161\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor c})\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\t(defn- ok-read\n   165\t  \"A scripted :ok read answer of `v` with successor cursor `c`.\"\n   166\t  [v c]\n   167\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   168\t   :dao.stream/value v :dao.stream/cursor c})\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t(defn- gap-read\n   172\t  \"A scripted :gap read answer with recovery cursor `c`.\"\n   173\t  [c]\n   174\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/gap :dao.stream/cursor c})\n   175\t\n   176\t\n   177\t;; =============================================================================\n   178\t;; apply-request\n   179\t;; =============================================================================\n   180\t\n   181\t(deftest apply-request-dispatches-each-operation-once\n   182\t  (let [h (ring 4)\n   183\t        c (:dao.stream/cursor\n   184\t            (mw/apply-request h {}\n   185\t                              {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   186\t                               :dao.stream.remote/args\n   187\t                               [:dao.stream/oldest]}))\n   188\t        a (mw/apply-request h {}\n   189\t                            {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   190\t                             :dao.stream.remote/args [:v]\n   191\t                             :dao.stream.test/open :kept})\n   192\t        n (mw/apply-request h {}\n   193\t                            {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   194\t                             :dao.stream.remote/args [c]})]\n   195\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome a)))\n   196\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome n)))\n   197\t    (is (= :v (:dao.stream/value n)))\n   198\t    (is (= (stream/next h c) n) \"the protocol call itself, verbatim\")\n   199\t    (testing \"an op outside the middleware vocabulary is a host assembly\n   200\t              defect and throws\"\n   201\t      (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs js/Error :cljd Object)\n   202\t            (mw/apply-request h {}\n   203\t                              {:dao.stream.remote/op\n   204\t                               :dao.stream/close!\n   205\t                               :dao.stream.remote/args []}))))))\n   206\t\n   207\t\n   208\t;; =============================================================================\n   209\t;; wrap: order, short-circuit, delegation, surfaces\n   210\t;; =============================================================================\n   211\t\n   212\t(deftest wrap-runs-ins-outermost-first-and-outs-innermost-outward\n   213\t  (let [calls (atom [])\n   214\t        log (atom [])\n   215\t        wrapped (mw/wrap (recording-handle calls)\n   216\t                         [(spy :a log pass-in pass-out)\n   217\t                          (spy :b log pass-in pass-out)])]\n   218\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   219\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :v))))\n   220\t    (is (= [[:in :a] [:in :b] [:out :b] [:out :a]] @log))\n   221\t    (is (= [[:append! :v]] @calls))))\n   222\t\n   223\t\n   224\t(deftest an-in-outcome-short-circuits-past-the-inner-handle\n   225\t  (let [calls (atom [])\n   226\t        log (atom [])\n   227\t        wrapped (mw/wrap (recording-handle calls)\n   228\t                         [(spy :a log pass-in pass-out)\n   229\t                          (spy :b log (refuse-in :b) pass-out)\n   230\t                          (spy :c log pass-in pass-out)])\n   231\t        outcome (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest)]\n   232\t    (is (= :dao.stream/refused (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)))\n   233\t    (is (= :b (:dao.stream.middleware/reason outcome)))\n   234\t    (is (= [] @calls) \"the inner handle is not consulted\")\n   235\t    (is (= [[:in :a] [:in :b] [:out :a]] @log)\n   236\t        \"only the middlewares outside b run their out transforms\")))\n   237\t\n   238\t\n   239\t(deftest descriptor-and-close-delegate-unchanged\n   240\t  (let [calls (atom [])\n   241\t        log (atom [])\n   242\t        h (recording-handle calls)\n   243\t        wrapped (mw/wrap h [(spy :a log pass-in pass-out)])]\n   244\t    (is (= (stream/descriptor h) (stream/descriptor wrapped)))\n   245\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   246\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/close! wrapped))))\n   247\t    (is (= [:descriptor :descriptor :close!] @calls))\n   248\t    (is (empty? @log) \"no middleware sees descriptor or close!\")))\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\t(deftest the-wrapped-handle-implements-exactly-the-inner-surfaces\n   252\t  (let [reader-only\n   253\t        (reify stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   254\t          (cursor\n   255\t            [_ _]\n   256\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   257\t             :dao.stream/cursor :c})\n   258\t\n   259\t          (next [_ _] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))]\n   260\t    (let [w (mw/wrap reader-only\n   261\t                     [(spy :a (atom []) pass-in pass-out)])]\n   262\t      (is (stream/descriptor? w))\n   263\t      (is (stream/reader? w))\n   264\t      (is (not (stream/writer? w)))\n   265\t      (is (not (stream/closable? w))))\n   266\t    (let [w (mw/wrap (ring 2)\n   267\t                     [(spy :a (atom []) pass-in pass-out)])]\n   268\t      (is (stream/reader? w))\n   269\t      (is (stream/writer? w))\n   270\t      (is (stream/closable? w)))))\n   271\t\n   272\t\n   273\t;; =============================================================================\n   274\t;; The position rule under a value cipher over a ring buffer\n   275\t;; =============================================================================\n   276\t\n   277\t(deftest a-value-cipher-preserves-positions-cursors-and-outcomes\n   278\t  (let [inner (ring 4)\n   279\t        wrapped (mw/wrap inner [(encryption)])]\n   280\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   281\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :v1))))\n   282\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   283\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :v2))))\n   284\t    (is (= [{:cipher/of :v1} {:cipher/of :v2}] (drain-values inner))\n   285\t        \"the inner handle stores only ciphertext\")\n   286\t    (let [cw (:dao.stream/cursor\n   287\t               (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest))\n   288\t          ci (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor inner :dao.stream/oldest))]\n   289\t      (is (= ci cw) \"the wrapped handle mints the inner handle's cursors\")\n   290\t      (let [rw (stream/next wrapped cw)\n   291\t            ri (stream/next inner ci)]\n   292\t        (is (= :v1 (:dao.stream/value rw))\n   293\t            \"the wrapped handle presents the plaintext\")\n   294\t        (is (= {:cipher/of :v1} (:dao.stream/value ri)))\n   295\t        (is (= (:dao.stream/cursor ri) (:dao.stream/cursor rw))\n   296\t            \"the successor cursor is the inner handle's own\")\n   297\t        (is (= (:dao.stream/outcome ri) (:dao.stream/outcome rw))\n   298\t            \"the outcome kind is untouched\"))))\n   299\t  (testing \"a gap crosses with the source's own recovery cursor\"\n   300\t    (let [inner (ring 2)\n   301\t          wrapped (mw/wrap inner [(encryption)])\n   302\t          ci (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor inner :dao.stream/oldest))\n   303\t          cw (:dao.stream/cursor\n   304\t               (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest))]\n   305\t      (is (= ci cw))\n   306\t      (doseq [v [:v1 :v2 :v3]]\n   307\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   308\t               (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped v)))))\n   309\t      (let [gi (stream/next inner ci)\n   310\t            gw (stream/next wrapped cw)]\n   311\t        (is (= :dao.stream/gap (:dao.stream/outcome gw)))\n   312\t        (is (= (:dao.stream/cursor gi) (:dao.stream/cursor gw))\n   313\t            \"the recovery cursor is the source's, unparsed and unrewritten\")\n   314\t        (let [rw (stream/next wrapped (:dao.stream/cursor gw))]\n   315\t          (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome rw)))\n   316\t          (is (= :v2 (:dao.stream/value rw))\n   317\t              \"the recovery read presents the retained plaintext\")\n   318\t          (is (= :v3 (:dao.stream/value\n   319\t                       (stream/next wrapped (:dao.stream/cursor rw))))\n   320\t              \"and the walk continues to the newest plaintext\"))))))\n   321\t\n   322\t\n   323\t(deftest an-undecodable-value-is-presented-as-the-marker\n   324\t  (let [inner (ring 4)\n   325\t        wrapped (mw/wrap inner [(encryption)])]\n   326\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   327\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! inner :raw))))\n   328\t    (let [c (:dao.stream/cursor\n   329\t              (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest))\n   330\t          plain (stream/next inner c)\n   331\t          r (stream/next wrapped c)]\n   332\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n   333\t      (is (= {:dao.stream.middleware/undecodable true\n   334\t              :dao.stream.middleware/raw :raw}\n   335\t             (:dao.stream/value r)))\n   336\t      (is (= (:dao.stream/cursor plain) (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   337\t          \"the cursor is untouched: the position is real\")\n   338\t      (is (= (:dao.stream/outcome plain) (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   339\t          \"the outcome is untouched: the reader decides\"))))\n   340\t\n   341\t\n   342\t(deftest an-untransformable-value-answers-invalid-value-on-the-way-in\n   343\t  (let [inner (ring 4)\n   344\t        encipher (fn [v]\n   345\t                   (if (= v :poison)\n   346\t                     (throw (ex-info \"cannot encode\" {:value v}))\n   347\t                     {:cipher/of v}))\n   348\t        wrapped (mw/wrap inner\n   349\t                         [(mw/encryption\n   350\t                            {:dao.stream.middleware/encipher encipher\n   351\t                             :dao.stream.middleware/decipher decipher})])]\n   352\t    (is (= :dao.stream/invalid-value\n   353\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :poison))))\n   354\t    (is (empty? (drain-values inner))\n   355\t        \"nothing reached the inner handle and nothing was appended\")))\n   356\t\n   357\t\n   358\t;; =============================================================================\n   359\t;; A filter cannot be expressed\n   360\t;; =============================================================================\n   361\t\n   362\t(deftest a-filter-cannot-be-expressed\n   363\t  (testing \"an out may replace a value, never remove the position\"\n   364\t    (let [inner (ring 4)\n   365\t          tombstone\n   366\t          (spy :filter (atom []) pass-in\n   367\t               (fn [_ctx _req outcome]\n   368\t                 (if (and (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome outcome))\n   369\t                          (= :drop (:dao.stream/value outcome)))\n   370\t                   (assoc outcome :dao.stream/value :dropped)\n   371\t                   outcome)))\n   372\t          wrapped (mw/wrap inner [tombstone])]\n   373\t      (doseq [v [:a :drop :c]]\n   374\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   375\t               (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped v)))))\n   376\t      (loop [cw (:dao.stream/cursor\n   377\t                  (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest))\n   378\t             ci (:dao.stream/cursor\n   379\t                  (stream/cursor inner :dao.stream/oldest))\n   380\t             seen []]\n   381\t        (let [rw (stream/next wrapped cw)\n   382\t              ri (stream/next inner ci)]\n   383\t          (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome rw))\n   384\t            (do (is (= (:dao.stream/cursor ri) (:dao.stream/cursor rw))\n   385\t                    \"the chain keeps the inner handle's positions\")\n   386\t                (recur (:dao.stream/cursor rw) (:dao.stream/cursor ri)\n   387\t                       (conj seen (:dao.stream/value rw))))\n   388\t            (is (= [:a :dropped :c] seen)\n   389\t                \"every element is still presented: dropping is not a\n   390\t                 transform's to decide\"))))))\n   391\t  (testing \"declining one element declines the whole operation\"\n   392\t    (let [inner (ring 4)\n   393\t          wrapped (mw/wrap inner\n   394\t                           [(spy :gate (atom []) (refuse-in :filtered)\n   395\t                                 pass-out)])]\n   396\t      (is (= :dao.stream/refused\n   397\t             (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :drop))))\n   398\t      (is (empty? (drain-values inner))\n   399\t          \"the stream holds nothing: a refusal is data, not a silent\n   400\t           skip\"))))\n   401\t\n   402\t\n   403\t(deftest an-out-that-violates-the-position-rule-raises\n   404\t  (testing \"an out that turns an ok from next into blocked raises\"\n   405\t    (let [inner (ring 4)\n   406\t          wrapped\n   407\t          (mw/wrap inner\n   408\t                   [(spy :filter (atom []) pass-in\n   409\t                         (fn [_ctx _req outcome]\n   410\t                           (if (= :drop (:dao.stream/value outcome))\n   411\t                             (assoc outcome :dao.stream/outcome\n   412\t                                    :dao.stream/blocked)\n   413\t                             outcome)))])]\n   414\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   415\t             (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :drop))))\n   416\t      (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs js/Error :cljd Object)\n   417\t            (stream/next\n   418\t              wrapped\n   419\t              (:dao.stream/cursor\n   420\t                (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest)))))\n   421\t      (is (= [:drop] (drain-values inner))\n   422\t          \"the element is still there: the chain raised and the stream\n   423\t           kept its sequence\")))\n   424\t  (testing \"an out that changes the outcome kind raises\"\n   425\t    (let [inner (ring 4)\n   426\t          wrapped\n   427\t          (mw/wrap inner\n   428\t                   [(spy :filter (atom []) pass-in\n   429\t                         (fn [_ctx _req _outcome]\n   430\t                           {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/refused}))])]\n   431\t      (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs js/Error :cljd Object)\n   432\t            (stream/append! wrapped :v)))))\n   433\t  (testing \"an out that rewrites a cursor raises\"\n   434\t    (let [inner (ring 4)\n   435\t          wrapped\n   436\t          (mw/wrap inner\n   437\t                   [(spy :filter (atom []) pass-in\n   438\t                         (fn [_ctx req outcome]\n   439\t                           (if (= :dao.stream/next\n   440\t                                  (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n   441\t                             (assoc outcome :dao.stream/cursor :forged)\n   442\t                             outcome)))])]\n   443\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   444\t             (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :v))))\n   445\t      (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs js/Error :cljd Object)\n   446\t            (stream/next\n   447\t              wrapped\n   448\t              (:dao.stream/cursor\n   449\t                (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest))))))))\n   450\t\n   451\t\n   452\t;; =============================================================================\n   453\t;; gate\n   454\t;; =============================================================================\n   455\t\n   456\t(deftest a-gate-with-the-channel-allow-list-refuses\n   457\t  (let [inner (ring 4)\n   458\t        wrapped (mw/wrap inner\n   459\t                         [(mw/gate\n   460\t                            {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   461\t                             (mw/channel-allow-list #{\"a\"})\n   462\t                             :dao.stream.middleware/decision (ring 1)})])]\n   463\t    (testing \"a channel on the list passes and the operation lands\"\n   464\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   465\t             (:dao.stream/outcome\n   466\t               (mw/apply-request wrapped\n   467\t                                 {:dao.stream.remote/channel \"a\"}\n   468\t                                 {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   469\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/args [:v]}))))\n   470\t      (is (= [:v] (drain-values inner))))\n   471\t    (testing \"a channel off the list is refused with its reason\"\n   472\t      (let [r (mw/apply-request wrapped\n   473\t                                {:dao.stream.remote/channel \"z\"}\n   474\t                                {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   475\t                                 :dao.stream.remote/args [:w]})]\n   476\t        (is (= :dao.stream/refused (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n   477\t        (is (= :dao.stream.middleware/channel-not-allowed\n   478\t               (:dao.stream.middleware/reason r))))\n   479\t      (is (= [:v] (drain-values inner)) \"nothing was appended\"))\n   480\t    (testing \"a local caller's {} context names no channel and refuses\"\n   481\t      (is (= :dao.stream/refused\n   482\t             (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :x)))))))\n   483\t\n   484\t\n   485\t(deftest a-gate-reads-the-latest-decision-through-a-capacity-1-medium\n   486\t  (let [medium (ring 1)\n   487\t        seen (atom [])\n   488\t        gate-mw (mw/gate\n   489\t                  {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   490\t                   (fn [d _ctx _req] (swap! seen conj d) nil)\n   491\t                   :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})\n   492\t        target (ring 4)\n   493\t        wrapped (mw/wrap target [gate-mw])\n   494\t        ;; One operation per gate pass: the cursor is the target's own,\n   495\t        ;; minted once, and every read! is one next through the gate.\n   496\t        c0 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor target :dao.stream/oldest))\n   497\t        read! (fn []\n   498\t                (mw/apply-request wrapped {}\n   499\t                                  {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   500\t                                   :dao.stream.remote/args [c0]}))]\n   501\t    (is (= :dao.stream/blocked (:dao.stream/outcome (read!))))\n   502\t    (is (= [{:dao.stream.middleware/none true}] @seen)\n   503\t        \"the medium has published nothing yet\")\n   504\t    (stream/append! medium :d1)\n   505\t    (read!)\n   506\t    (is (= [{:dao.stream.middleware/none true} :d1] @seen))\n   507\t    ;; Two further decisions evict :d1; the gate's cursor spans the\n   508\t    ;; eviction of :d2 as well.\n   509\t    (stream/append! medium :d2)\n   510\t    (stream/append! medium :d3)\n   511\t    (read!)\n   512\t    (is (= [{:dao.stream.middleware/none true} :d1 :d3] @seen)\n   513\t        \"the latest decision, recovered through the eviction\")))\n   514\t\n   515\t\n   516\t(deftest the-gate-decision-read-lifecycle\n   517\t  (testing \"the definition mints nothing; each wrap mints its own\"\n   518\t    (let [calls (atom [])\n   519\t          gate-mw\n   520\t          (mw/gate\n   521\t            {:dao.stream.middleware/verify (fn [_ _ _] nil)\n   522\t             :dao.stream.middleware/decision\n   523\t             (scripted-medium calls\n   524\t                              (atom [(ok-cursor :c0) (ok-cursor :c1)])\n   525\t                              (atom [{:dao.stream/outcome\n   526\t                                      :dao.stream/blocked}\n   527\t                                     {:dao.stream/outcome\n   528\t                                      :dao.stream/blocked}]))})]\n   529\t      (is (= [] @calls) \"a definition is inert: no state, no mint\")\n   530\t      (let [wrapped-a (mw/wrap (recording-handle (atom [])) [gate-mw])]\n   531\t        (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest]] @calls)\n   532\t            \"the first wrap mints once, at wrap\")\n   533\t        (let [wrapped-b (mw/wrap (recording-handle (atom [])) [gate-mw])]\n   534\t          (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest]\n   535\t                  [:cursor :dao.stream/oldest]] @calls)\n   536\t              \"the same definition mints again for the second wrap\")\n   537\t          (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   538\t                 (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/next wrapped-a :c))))\n   539\t          (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   540\t                 (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/next wrapped-b :c))))\n   541\t          (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest]\n   542\t                  [:cursor :dao.stream/oldest]\n   543\t                  [:next :c0] [:next :c1]] @calls)\n   544\t              \"each wrapped handle reads the shared medium through its\n   545\t               own minted cursor\")))))\n   546\t  (testing \"a mint that never answers ok leaves verify the none marker\"\n   547\t    (let [calls (atom [])\n   548\t          medium (scripted-medium\n   549\t                   calls\n   550\t                   (atom [{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error}\n   551\t                          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error}])\n   552\t                   (atom []))\n   553\t          seen (atom [])\n   554\t          gate-mw (mw/gate\n   555\t                    {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   556\t                     (fn [d _ctx _req] (swap! seen conj d) nil)\n   557\t                     :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})\n   558\t          inner-calls (atom [])\n   559\t          wrapped (mw/wrap (recording-handle inner-calls) [gate-mw])]\n   560\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   561\t             (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/next wrapped :my-c))))\n   562\t      (is (= [{:dao.stream.middleware/none true}] @seen))\n   563\t      (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest] [:cursor :dao.stream/oldest]] @calls)\n   564\t          \"the wrap mint, then one retry this operation; next is skipped\")\n   565\t      (is (= [[:next :my-c]] @inner-calls)\n   566\t          \"the request itself passes through unchanged\")))\n   567\t  (testing \"blocked keeps the cursor and the last value\"\n   568\t    (let [calls (atom [])\n   569\t          medium (scripted-medium calls\n   570\t                                  (atom [(ok-cursor :c0)])\n   571\t                                  (atom [(ok-read :d1 :c1)\n   572\t                                         {:dao.stream/outcome\n   573\t                                          :dao.stream/blocked}]))\n   574\t          seen (atom [])\n   575\t          wrapped (mw/wrap (ring 4)\n   576\t                           [(mw/gate\n   577\t                              {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   578\t                               (fn [d _ctx _req] (swap! seen conj d) nil)\n   579\t                               :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})])]\n   580\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   581\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   582\t      (is (= [:d1 :d1] @seen) \"the last value is kept across blocked\")\n   583\t      (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest] [:next :c0] [:next :c1]] @calls)\n   584\t          \"next is called once per operation\")))\n   585\t  (testing \"end ends the gate: no later operation reads the medium\"\n   586\t    (let [calls (atom [])\n   587\t          medium (scripted-medium calls\n   588\t                                  (atom [(ok-cursor :c0)])\n   589\t                                  (atom [{:dao.stream/outcome\n   590\t                                          :dao.stream/end}]))\n   591\t          seen (atom [])\n   592\t          wrapped (mw/wrap (ring 4)\n   593\t                           [(mw/gate\n   594\t                              {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   595\t                               (fn [d _ctx _req] (swap! seen conj d) nil)\n   596\t                               :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})])]\n   597\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   598\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   599\t      (is (= [{:dao.stream.middleware/ended true}\n   600\t              {:dao.stream.middleware/ended true}] @seen))\n   601\t      (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest] [:next :c0]] @calls)\n   602\t          \"the ended gate reads no more\")))\n   603\t  (testing \"one recovery read after a gap, then the latest value\"\n   604\t    (let [calls (atom [])\n   605\t          medium (scripted-medium calls\n   606\t                                  (atom [(ok-cursor :c0)])\n   607\t                                  (atom [(gap-read :c9)\n   608\t                                         (ok-read :d2 :c10)\n   609\t                                         {:dao.stream/outcome\n   610\t                                          :dao.stream/blocked}]))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
