{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/middleware.cljc | sed -n '388,650p'\"","aggregated_output":"   388\t(defn gate\n   389\t  \"The authorize step: `(gate {:dao.stream.middleware/verify verify\n   390\t   :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})` -> middleware definition.\n   391\t   `wrap` mints the gate's state once per wrapped handle and, minting\n   392\t   it, calls `cursor` :oldest on the decision medium once: the read\n   393\t   cursor and the last value are state of the wrapped handle, so one\n   394\t   definition may be wrapped over many handles, each with its own\n   395\t   cursor. Each operation retries the mint once when it has no cursor,\n   396\t   then calls `next` on the medium once, plus the one recovery re-read\n   397\t   after a gap; when the medium answers end the gate becomes ended and\n   398\t   reads no more. `verify` is `(fn [decision ctx req] -> nil |\n   399\t   reason)`, the adapter contract of dao.shibi.md: nil passes the\n   400\t   request through; a reason short-circuits with :dao.stream/refused.\n   401\t   Serialize calls on one wrapped handle; the gate has no queue, lock\n   402\t   or wait.\"\n   403\t  [opts]\n   404\t  (let [verify (:dao.stream.middleware/verify opts)\n   405\t        decision (:dao.stream.middleware/decision opts)\n   406\t        blank {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? false}\n   407\t        mint!\n   408\t        (fn []\n   409\t          (let [r (stream/cursor decision stream/anchor-oldest)]\n   410\t            (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   411\t              (:dao.stream/cursor r))))\n   412\t\n   413\t        store! (fn [state s] (vreset! state s) s)\n   414\t\n   415\t        absorb\n   416\t        (fn [s r]\n   417\t          (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   418\t            :dao.stream/ok\n   419\t            {:cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r) :value? true\n   420\t             :value (:dao.stream/value r) :ended? false}\n   421\t\n   422\t            :dao.stream/blocked s\n   423\t\n   424\t            :dao.stream/end\n   425\t            {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? true}\n   426\t\n   427\t            :dao.stream/gap\n   428\t            ;; One recovery re-read; never a third read this operation.\n   429\t            (let [rec (:dao.stream/cursor r)\n   430\t                  r2 (stream/next decision rec)]\n   431\t              (case (:dao.stream/outcome r2)\n   432\t                :dao.stream/ok\n   433\t                {:cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r2) :value? true\n   434\t                 :value (:dao.stream/value r2) :ended? false}\n   435\t\n   436\t                :dao.stream/blocked\n   437\t                {:cursor rec :value? false :value nil :ended? false}\n   438\t\n   439\t                :dao.stream/end\n   440\t                {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? true}\n   441\t\n   442\t                ;; A recovery gap adopts the recovery cursor and stays\n   443\t                ;; without a value.\n   444\t                :dao.stream/gap\n   445\t                {:cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r2) :value? false\n   446\t                 :value nil :ended? false}\n   447\t\n   448\t                ;; Any other recovery outcome clears cursor and value;\n   449\t                ;; the mint is retried afresh next operation.\n   450\t                {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? false}))\n   451\t\n   452\t            ;; Any other non-ok outcome clears value and cursor; the\n   453\t            ;; mint is retried afresh next operation.\n   454\t            {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? false}))\n   455\t\n   456\t        latest\n   457\t        (fn [state]\n   458\t          (let [s0 @state]\n   459\t            (if (:ended? s0)\n   460\t              ended-marker\n   461\t              (do\n   462\t                (when-not (:cursor s0)\n   463\t                  (when-let [c (mint!)]\n   464\t                    (store! state (assoc s0 :cursor c))))\n   465\t                (let [s1 @state]\n   466\t                  (when (:cursor s1)\n   467\t                    (store! state (absorb s1 (stream/next decision\n   468\t                                                          (:cursor s1)))))\n   469\t                  (let [s2 @state]\n   470\t                    (cond (:ended? s2) ended-marker\n   471\t                          (:value? s2) (:value s2)\n   472\t                          :else none-marker)))))))]\n   473\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/state\n   474\t     (fn []\n   475\t       (let [state (volatile! blank)]\n   476\t         (when-let [c (mint!)]\n   477\t           (vswap! state assoc :cursor c))\n   478\t         state))\n   479\t     :dao.stream.middleware/in\n   480\t     (fn [state ctx req]\n   481\t       (let [reason (verify (latest state) ctx req)]\n   482\t         (if (nil? reason)\n   483\t           req\n   484\t           {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/refused\n   485\t            :dao.stream.middleware/reason reason})))\n   486\t     :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   487\t     (fn [_state _ctx _req outcome] outcome)}))\n   488\t\n   489\t\n   490\t;; =============================================================================\n   491\t;; present, the credential step\n   492\t;; =============================================================================\n   493\t\n   494\t(defn present\n   495\t  \"The credential step: `(present {:dao.stream.middleware/present f})`\n   496\t   -> middleware, where `f` is `(fn [ctx req] -> credential)`. Its `in`\n   497\t   associates the result under :dao.stream.remote/credential on the\n   498\t   operation map; its `out` is identity.\"\n   499\t  [opts]\n   500\t  (let [present-fn (:dao.stream.middleware/present opts)]\n   501\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   502\t     (fn [ctx req]\n   503\t       (assoc req :dao.stream.remote/credential (present-fn ctx req)))\n   504\t     :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   505\t     (fn [_ctx _req outcome] outcome)}))\n   506\t\n   507\t\n   508\t;; =============================================================================\n   509\t;; Exemplars\n   510\t;; =============================================================================\n   511\t\n   512\t(defn encryption\n   513\t  \"The spec's value-encryption exemplar. `encipher` and `decipher` come\n   514\t   from a library cipher; the key is an argument to whatever built them.\n   515\t   `in` on append! replaces the value with its ciphertext, answering\n   516\t   :dao.stream/invalid-value when the value cannot be transformed on the\n   517\t   way in. `out` on an ok from next replaces :dao.stream/value with the\n   518\t   plaintext or, when it cannot be transformed on the way out, with\n   519\t   {:dao.stream.middleware/undecodable true :dao.stream.middleware/raw\n   520\t   v}, the outcome and cursor untouched. Cursors are never touched.\"\n   521\t  [opts]\n   522\t  (let [encipher (:dao.stream.middleware/encipher opts)\n   523\t        decipher (:dao.stream.middleware/decipher opts)]\n   524\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   525\t     (fn [_ctx req]\n   526\t       (if (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n   527\t         (try\n   528\t           (update-in req [:dao.stream.remote/args 0] encipher)\n   529\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) _\n   530\t             {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-value}))\n   531\t         req))\n   532\t     :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   533\t     (fn [_ctx req outcome]\n   534\t       (if (and (= :dao.stream/next (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n   535\t                (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)))\n   536\t         (try\n   537\t           (update outcome :dao.stream/value decipher)\n   538\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) _\n   539\t             (assoc outcome :dao.stream/value\n   540\t                    {:dao.stream.middleware/undecodable true\n   541\t                     :dao.stream.middleware/raw\n   542\t                     (:dao.stream/value outcome)})))\n   543\t         outcome))}))\n   544\t\n   545\t\n   546\t(defn metering\n   547\t  \"The spec's metering exemplar: `out` appends {:meter/identity id\n   548\t   :meter/op op :meter/outcome kind} to the composed metering stream\n   549\t   `sink` and returns the outcome unchanged. The side effect is a\n   550\t   stream emission, never a retry or a wait.\"\n   551\t  [opts]\n   552\t  (let [sink (:meter/stream opts)\n   553\t        id (:meter/identity opts)]\n   554\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   555\t     (fn [_ctx req] req)\n   556\t     :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   557\t     (fn [_ctx req outcome]\n   558\t       (stream/append! sink\n   559\t                       {:meter/identity id\n   560\t                        :meter/op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n   561\t                        :meter/outcome (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)})\n   562\t       outcome)}))\n   563\t\n   564\t\n   565\t;; =============================================================================\n   566\t;; The trivial policy this repository ships with\n   567\t;; =============================================================================\n   568\t\n   569\t(defn channel-allow-list\n   570\t  \"An allow-list `verify` for `gate`, keyed on\n   571\t   :dao.stream.remote/channel in ctx and ignoring the credential and the\n   572\t   decision: nil for a channel identity in `allowed`, a refusal reason\n   573\t   for anything else, a missing channel included. The reason vocabulary\n   574\t   itself belongs to dao.shibi.md; this one is composition-owned.\"\n   575\t  [allowed]\n   576\t  (fn [_decision ctx _req]\n   577\t    (if (contains? allowed (:dao.stream.remote/channel ctx))\n   578\t      nil\n   579\t      :dao.stream.middleware/channel-not-allowed)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'undecodable|position|metering|gate|short.circuit|non-ok|outcome' docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md | head -110\"","aggregated_output":"12:map on the way in and one over the outcome map on the way out. Each\n14:three bounded exceptions named below: the gate's read on its composed\n16:only by the gate itself), a metering emission to a composed side stream,\n17:and the gate's one recovery re-read after a gap. These are stream\n22:response pair maps onto the operation map and the contract's outcome map.\n25:{:dao.stream.middleware/in  (fn [ctx req] -> req | outcome-map)\n26: :dao.stream.middleware/out (fn [ctx req outcome] -> outcome)}\n29:`in` returning an outcome map short-circuits: the inner handle is not\n30:consulted and that map is the operation's outcome, after the `out`\n47:is a name and `close!` is a lifecycle transition, and neither has an outcome\n50:`(apply-request h ctx req) -> outcome` applies one operation map to a\n60:outward. Its `descriptor` and `close!` delegate to `h` unchanged.\n66:## The position rule\n68:A middleware maps position `p` of the inner handle to position `p` of the\n73:- changes `:dao.stream/outcome`, `:dao.stream/identity`,\n79:short-circuit with an outcome from the operation's exhaustive set. A cipher,\n82:stream with its own identity (`dao.stream.md`, Composition), never a\n90:read `gate` defines below (a bounded read on a composed decision medium,\n92:a non-`ok` outcome mints afresh next operation; neither retries the\n101:A value that cannot be transformed on the way out (undecodable ciphertext,\n103:`{:dao.stream.middleware/undecodable true :dao.stream.middleware/raw v}`\n104:under `:dao.stream/value`, with the outcome and cursor untouched: the\n105:position is real and the reader decides. A value that cannot be transformed\n110:**gate**, the authorize step. Composition data only; the policy is not\n114:(gate {:dao.stream.middleware/verify   verify\n118:The decision medium is written by an interpreter the composition runs over\n120:own cadence, and appends each derived decision. Neither the gate nor the\n122:whatever value the index publishes; the gate reads none of it. It may be an\n127:plugs into the gate (`dao.shibi.md`, How it plugs in).\n130:the gate. The medium must be open and readable; it has capacity one and\n131:evicts its older value. If cursor minting is not `ok`, the gate has no read\n136:On each operation, the gate calls `next` once at its read cursor. On `ok`,\n143:not read a third time in this operation. On any other non-`ok` outcome,\n148:`{:dao.stream.middleware/ended true}` once the gate is ended (the medium\n151:`nil` passes the request through; a reason short-circuits with\n152:`{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/refused\n155:wrapped handle, supplied to `wrap`, not global state. The composition must\n156:serialize calls on one wrapped handle; the gate has no queue, lock or wait.\n157:The decision medium is not the wrapped stream, so the position rule on the\n160:A gate that must account for its own decisions appends each as\n164:rather than in the gate.\n184:`:dao.stream/value` with the plaintext or the undecodable marker. Cursors\n189:Metering: `out` appends `{:meter/identity id :meter/op op :meter/outcome\n190:kind}` to a composed metering stream and returns the outcome unchanged. The\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
