{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.md | sed -n '560,585p'\"","aggregated_output":"   560\t  cursor is how a reader detaches — there is nothing to unregister.\n   561\t- Because cursors are immutable values, a reader may retain an old cursor and\n   562\t  re-read retained history, or hand a cursor to another interpreter. What a\n   563\t  cursor can still observe is governed only by retention.\n   564\t\n   565\t## Reading\n   566\t\n   567\t`next` takes a handle and a cursor and returns an outcome immediately.\n   568\tIt is total and non-blocking: every state of the stream has a defined data\n   569\tanswer.\n   570\t\n   571\t| Outcome                       | Meaning                                                                       | Required keys                                                                           |\n   572\t|-------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n   573\t| `:dao.stream/ok`              | A value was observed.                                                         | `:dao.stream/value`, `:dao.stream/cursor` (successor)                                   |\n   574\t| `:dao.stream/blocked`         | Nothing at this position yet; retry later.                                    | —                                                                                       |\n   575\t| `:dao.stream/end`             | What this handle is on is closed and this position is past the retained tail. | —                                                                                       |\n   576\t| `:dao.stream/gap`             | This position was evicted.                                                    | `:dao.stream/cursor` (earliest retained position, or the tail when nothing is retained) |\n   577\t| `:dao.stream/cursor-mismatch` | The cursor was minted by a different logical stream.                          | —                                                                                       |\n   578\t| `:dao.stream/invalid-cursor`  | The value is not a cursor.                                                    | —                                                                                       |\n   579\t| `:dao.stream/refused`         | A policy composed on this handle declined the read; nothing was observed.     | —                                                                                       |\n   580\t| `:dao.stream/transport-error` | The transport failed to perform the read; nothing was observed.               | —                                                                                       |\n   581\t\n   582\tReading never mutates the stream. Two readers with cursors at the same\n   583\tposition observe the same retained value; neither can starve or affect the\n   584\tother. There is no destructive read anywhere in the contract — no drain, no\n   585\ttake. An operation that removes an element as it reads would make one\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
