{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 01:06:50 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-27 08:06:50 ICT\n\nP1 | [middleware.cljc:96](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/middleware.cljc:96) | The position check compares protected keys with `get`. Adding a previously absent `:dao.stream/cursor`, `:dao.stream/anchor`, identity, op, or id with a `nil` value passes that comparison, despite the stated rule that adding those keys is a change. The same gap permits adding `:dao.stream/value nil` to a non-`ok` outcome. | Compare key presence as well as values for protected keys and for value when replacement is forbidden. Add adversarial tests for absent-to-`nil` additions.\n\nThe per-wrap gate state and recovery handling match the specified lifecycle. Nested wraps and short circuits follow the expected transform order. The encryption marker replaces a value on an `ok` from `next`, so it passes the intended rule. Validation scans outcome keys on each `out`, including metering; that is linear in outcome-map size, but I found no separate correctness defect there. I did not rerun the supplied suites or edit files.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED"}}
